5% range +0.13 to +0.27), about +2.6\u00b0F since 1895.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Tucson's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.05 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 10.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1905 (24.17 in); the driest, 2020 (4.17 in). Tucson almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.2 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 15 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}